    <string name="guard_router_router_help_password">Enter the OpenWrt administrator password. The usual login is root; this is not the Wi-Fi password.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_pin">Choose your own four-digit PIN during first setup. Use that PIN to connect to a configured router. After manual package installation, set the PIN in LuCI using the owner account. There is no preset PIN.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_profile">Choose a phone profile to send to the router, or add one later.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_protocols">Choose the released protocols used by your VPN profiles. Hysteria2 is selected when available. More protocols can be added after pairing the router.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_public_ip">Choose this only if the router can be reached from the internet through a public IP. A mobile-network check is still required.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_reset_foxhole">Removes only FoxHole settings, its PIN and client records. Set up FoxHole again afterward. OpenWrt and other apps keep their settings.</string>
    <string name="guard_router_router_help_setup_pair">Install adds FoxHole to a supported OpenWrt router. Connect pairs this phone with an existing FoxHole installation. OpenWrt firmware is not installed or upgraded.</string>
